Focuses the warning before http's button only while the warning shows. Chrome
focuses it as the dialog is made, even for a tab that isn't showing, whose
dialog the tab dialog manager shows inactive and hides at once. The core gives
a tab's dialog a window of its own on Windows (PageDialogsInOwnWindow), and
focusing a view in a hidden window activates it there, so an agent's tab at
the warning took the keyboard from the user's window (#3164). The inactive
show already stores the button for the dialog's activation, which focuses it
as the tab comes forward.

--- a/chrome/browser/ssl/ask_before_http_dialog_controller.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ssl/ask_before_http_dialog_controller.cc
@@ -254,7 +254,14 @@
   // Explicitly call RequestFocus() to ensure initially focused view is focused.
   views::View* focused_view = model_host->GetInitiallyFocusedView();
   CHECK(focused_view);
-  focused_view->RequestFocus();
+  // browser_core: only while the dialog shows. A dialog of a tab that isn't
+  // showing was shown inactive, which stored this view for its activation, and
+  // hidden. Focusing a view in it activates its hidden window on Windows, where
+  // the dialog is a window of its own, so it took the keyboard from the window
+  // the user was in (#3164).
+  if (dialog_widget_->IsVisible()) {
+    focused_view->RequestFocus();
+  }
 #else
   current_dialog_model_ = dialog_model.get();
   ui::ModalDialogWrapper::ShowTabModal(std::move(dialog_model), window);
